   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package entry point for exllamav3. It sets environment defaults before importing PyTorch (disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread by default), raises a clear error if PyTorch is missing, and configures CUDA allocator settings (expandable segments) and the Triton backend for ROCm where appropriate. It then re-exports the library's main public API\u2014`Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `Cache`, `Generator`, and related classes\u2014so users can access them directly from the top-level package."
  },
