   "finish": "stop",
   "text_sha256": "0149946ba8846c4a61037c1fb42ef7488126739462ddf2b9842058ddce72b2d3",
   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe very first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package's top-level entry point. It sets environment defaults before importing torch (disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread and pointing Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds), configures the CUDA caching allocator to use expandable segments unless the user has already set `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF` or is on Windows/ROCm, raises a helpful error if torch isn't installed, and then re-exports the library's public API \u2014 `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `MMEmbedding`, the cache classes, and the generator/sampler classes \u2014 so users can import them directly from `exllamav3`."
  },
