   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe very first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package entry point for exllamav3. It sets environment defaults before importing torch (disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread, enabling expandable CUDA allocator segments, and pointing Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds), raises a helpful error if PyTorch is missing, and then re-exports the library's public API \u2014 `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `MMEmbedding`, the cache classes, and the generator/job/filter/sampler classes \u2014 so users can import them directly from `exllamav3`."
